+---
+title: Adding a built-in ParamType (click.Duration)
+author: HarzerHeribert
+date: 2026-10-15
+cost: { minutes: 2, tokens: 60416 }
+touches:
+  - CHANGES.md
+  - docs/api.md
+  - docs/parameter-types.md
+  - src/click/__init__.py
+  - src/click/types.py
+  - tests/test_types.py
+---
+
+## Decided
+- A new built-in type touches 5 places: the class in src/click/types.py (next to a similar type, with `name`, `convert`, `__repr__`), the export in src/click/__init__.py (alphabetical `from .types import X as X`), an `autoclass` entry in docs/api.md, an example section plus a listing entry in docs/parameter-types.md, and a changelog entry in CHANGES.md under a new "Version X.Y.0 / Unreleased" heading.
+- The metavar comes from `name.upper()`, and `to_info_dict` derives `param_type` from the class name, so a plain subclass needs no `get_metavar` or `to_info_dict` override.
+- Duration: plain digits mean seconds (`isascii() and isdigit()`, so Unicode digits are rejected); otherwise it uses `fullmatch` on an optional d/h/m/s regex with IGNORECASE. Non-str, non-timedelta values fail as the spec requires (so `default=120` as an int fails).
+- Failure messages use `_("{value!r} is not a valid ...").format(value=value)` through `self.fail`, the same pattern as UUID.
+
+## Tried and ruled out
+- Making the bare number an optional trailing `s?` on the seconds group: it would wrongly accept "1h30" as 1h30s.
+
+## Watch out
+- The d/h/m/s regex matches the empty string, so guard against `""` explicitly.
+- `timedelta(days=huge)` raises OverflowError and `int()` of very long digit strings raises ValueError; catch both and call `self.fail`.
+- The bench venv has no ruff or mypy; pyright is on PATH. In zsh, `echo ===` errors, so use `echo '---'` as a separator.
